2026-11-13T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2492) 'the motion matching guest predicts a body on the wire
 # uuid: 41071212-cd58-543d-a4e6-24afca0afa2e
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l1
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-13T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2492) 'a sender states a clip and a time and sends only what the guest cannot predict.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2492) 'the presence slice's frame codec: a predictor under Zstandard, its gates and controls.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Both ends of a presence stream hold the same clips and the same motion matching guest. How many
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2492) 'bytes of a body does a sender still have to send?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2492) 'A person's body goes on the wire as 21 entity Packets of 100 bytes, in two frames of 12, once
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2492) 'every 6 ticks of a 64 Hz clock. Each frame is coded alone against one fixed dictionary.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Measured on 62 clips, that stream is 8,693 bytes a second at level 19, which is 6% over the
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2492) 'sustained budget of 8,192. A dictionary cannot close the gap: coding a frame against the send
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2492) 'before it saves 3%. But the body is not free motion. The stick feeds `mm_step`, which answers a
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2492) 'clip and a time, and the body is that clip's pose placed in the world. A viewer that runs the
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2492) 'same guest on the same clips can make most of that pose itself.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Run the frame size tool on the 62 clips with the predictor in the codec and without it. The
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2492) 'rung passes when the bytes a second with the predictor are below the 8,693 of the fixed
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2492) 'dictionary on the same sends, the decoded frames equal the frames that were sent, bit for bit,
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2492) 'and each of the four controls below is caught.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2492) 'the motion matching guest predicts a body on the wire
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The predictor is the motion matching guest, `mm.elf` (operator, 2026-11-13: "he motion
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2492) '  matching guest yes."). No learned model is brought in before this has been tried.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The predictor sits in the frame codec, under Zstandard. A decoded frame is still 12 whole
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2492) '  Packets of 100 bytes, so the Packet layout does not change and the observers hash the same
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2492) '  frames as today.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The clip and the time travel in the payload of a Packet that is already sent. Nothing travels
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2492) '  beside the Packets.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Every send states its own clip and time. A frame stands alone, and a lost send does not make
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2492) '  the next one unreadable.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The hash of the clip set and of the guest joins the hashes of the dictionary and of the part
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2492) '  table as one protocol version. A viewer with another version is refused.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2492) '- RFD66606-2436, presence, the slice this codec serves.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2492) '- RFD66606-2442 and RFD66606-2443, the latency metric and the server that carries the frames.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

