 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2492) '  for frames and Packets, `docs/frame-sizes.md` for the measurement this RFD must beat,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2492) '  `docs/ledger.md` with `ledger.tsv` for how a rung is recorded, and `tools/frame_sizes.exs`,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2492) '  the tool that measures any recorded stream. The parts it joins are repositories of their
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2492) '  own beside it; the Packet codec is interactor-packets-guest and RFD66606-2493 names the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2492) '  rest.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The motion matching guest's repository, interactor-motion-matching-guest, which the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2492) '  workspace checks out on its interactor side. Its README has `mm_add_clip`, `mm_bake` and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2492) '  `mm_step(dt, vx, vz, facing, mode, jump)`, which answers a clip, a time, the character and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2492) '  the clip root for each frame.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The packet contract, contract-entity-packet. A Packet is 100 bytes: `gid` at 0, position in
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2492) '  micrometres at 4, velocity at 28, acceleration at 34, the tick at 40, rotation at 52 and 40
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2492) '  bytes of payload at 58.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The avatar follower, interactor-anny-follow-guest. `follow.sgd` and `data/drive.tsv` hold
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2492) '  the 21 bodies of the muscle skeleton that drive ANNY. Their order on the wire is
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2492) '  `data/parts.tsv` of the codec's repository, a whole coarse body in the first frame.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2492) 'What was measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2492) 'The 62 clips that pass the retarget gates, 29 minutes of motion, were played at the tick and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2492) 'written as the frames one person would send. Half the clips built the dictionary and sends of
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2492) 'the other half were measured.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2492) '| Cadence | Dictionary | Level | Bytes a send | Bytes a second |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2492) '| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2492) '| 6 ticks | none | 3 | 982 | 10,476 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2492) '| 6 ticks | fixed, 64 KiB | 3 | 947 | 10,100 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2492) '| 6 ticks | fixed, 64 KiB | 19 | 815 | 8,693 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2492) '| 6 ticks | the send before | 19 | 791 | 8,436 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2492) '| 8 ticks | fixed, 64 KiB | 19 | 814 | 6,510 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2492) 'The row to beat is the third. The fourth shows why a better dictionary is not the way: the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2492) 'best possible one, the send before, gains 3%.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Why a predictor should work here
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2492) 'A body in this slice is made in a chain. The left stick sets a wanted ground velocity. The
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2492) 'motion matching guest picks a clip and a time. The clip's pose at that time is placed in the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2492) 'world, and the muscle skeleton takes it. So for a sender whose body follows the guest, clip,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2492) 'time and root placement fix the pose of most of the 21 parts. What they do not fix is what the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2492) 'guest cannot know: the tracked head and hands, and what physics adds.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:14Z (RFD66606-2492) 'No number is claimed for the saving. A rough bound, if only the head and two hands carried
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:15Z (RFD66606-2492) 'information beyond clip, time and root, is 150 to 250 bytes a send against 815. It is a guess
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-2492) 'until the first rung measures it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:18Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Loss is another matter
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:19Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Zstandard is not an error-correcting code and is not used as one. Compression removes
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-2492) 'redundancy and a code for errors adds it. Loss is concealed by the curve a viewer already
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-2492) 'draws: one lost send costs nothing, and after three a part moves 7% over its top speed for one
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-2492) 'segment. A third interval of playback delay is the first remedy if loss hurts. RFD66606-2327
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-2492) 'has the gait phase the guest matches by, and RFD66606-2363 the controllers that feed it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-2492) 'The ladder
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Each rung is held to the rung below it and not to the budget. The budget is where the ladder
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-2492) 'ends.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Rungs are climbed in this order and none is skipped. A rung is the run of the rung below with
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-2492) 'one thing changed. It is run on the development machine before anything is pushed, and it
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-2492) 'passes when its number is better than the rung below while its controls are caught.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:32Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:33Z (RFD66606-2492) '0. Run `tools/frame_sizes.exs` as it is on the 62 clips. Nothing has to improve: it must give
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:34Z (RFD66606-2492) '   8,693 again, so that the baseline is this session's own.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:35Z (RFD66606-2492) '1. The guest's digest on four hosts, as the MuJoCo guest has. Hosts that agree on `mm_step`
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:36Z (RFD66606-2492) '   go from 0 to 4.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:37Z (RFD66606-2492) '2. Residual frames: each Packet's fields less the predicted pose, for clips played back as
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:38Z (RFD66606-2492) '   they are. Bytes a second go below rung 0.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:39Z (RFD66606-2492) '3. Clip and time in a payload, and the decoder that rebuilds the frame from them. Frames
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:40Z (RFD66606-2492) '   rebuilt bit for bit go from none to all.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:41Z (RFD66606-2492) '4. A body that strays from the clip: head and hands on a recorded track. Bytes a second are
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:42Z (RFD66606-2492) '   set against rung 2 and reported as they are.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:43Z (RFD66606-2492) '5. The codec as a sandbox guest beside `curve.sgd`. Its bytes equal the tool's.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:44Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:45Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Rung 1 comes before any coding because a predictor that differs between two machines by one
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:46Z (RFD66606-2492) 'bit makes every decoded frame wrong. The MuJoCo guest already has a digest on Linux x86_64,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:47Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Linux arm64, Windows x86_64 and macOS arm64, with the in-process JIT switched off, and that
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:48Z (RFD66606-2492) 'check found a defect on its first day.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:49Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:50Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Gates and controls
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:51Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Each gate prints a `RESULT:` line, and each control plants a defect that must be caught and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:52Z (RFD66606-2492) 'named.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:53Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:54Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Round trip: every frame that is coded decodes to the bytes that were sent. Control: one bit
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:55Z (RFD66606-2492) '  of the residual flipped.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:56Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Alone: a frame decodes with no other frame at hand. Control: a decoder that keeps the clip
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:57Z (RFD66606-2492) '  and time of the send before, which must fail when a send is withheld.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:58Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Version: a viewer whose clip set differs is refused by name. Control: one clip altered.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:59Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Bytes: the stream is smaller than the rung below on the same sends. Control: a predictor that
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:00Z (RFD66606-2492) '  answers the rest pose, which must give no saving.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:01Z (RFD66606-2492) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:02:02Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Rules a new session must keep
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
